Subject: [PATCH 021/230] Keep prediction windows live and surface them in
 history and pushes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Countdowns were frozen at render, the open-first list reshuffled on every
tick, the history page couldn't tell an open pick from a closed one, and the
lineup push only announced the XI. Windows now come from one server
definition reused by the write gate, the history read and the bot; a ticking
clock keeps hub and history countdowns honest; the list re-ranks only when
the picture changes; and the lineup push fires on the robust published signal
and names every mechanic it opens.

